 "issue": 95,
 "issue_title": "Angle, wavelength, and length unit inconsistency",
 "issue_body": "\n- `ray_tracer.py` uses radians.\n- `aberrations.py` uses degrees (`field_angle_deg`).\n- `transform.py:61` uses degrees for Euler angles.\n- `ray_tracer.py` uses mm for wavelengths (`WAVELENGTH_GREEN * NM_TO_MM`).\n- `aberrations.py` uses nm.\n- `diffraction.py:74` uses **metres**.\n\nThis is the kind of inconsistency that causes silent factor\u2011of\u20111000 bugs. Adopt unit suffixes (`wavelength_nm`, `angle_rad`) on any public function that doesn't fix the unit in the name.\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/95",
 "pr": 116,
 "pr_title": "Standardize physical units and flat surface sentinels across codebase",
